1
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:13,980
You cannot imagine how the name of Robben Island made us afraid.

2
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:17,560
It was a prison from which no one escaped.

3
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:22,200
There I spent the hardest time of my life.

4
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:27,140
But when I got there Nelson Mandela was also there and he helped me.

5
00:00:27,140 --> 00:00:32,340
Mr Mandela began a school for those of us who had little learning.

6
00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:38,360
He taught us during the lunch breaks and the evenings when we should have been asleep.

7
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:46,220
We read books under our blankets and used anything we could find to make candles to see the words.

8
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:48,900
I became a good student.

9
00:00:49,380 --> 00:00:54,480
I wanted to study for my degree but I was not allowed to do that.

10
00:00:55,460 --> 00:00:59,320
Later, Mr Mandela allowed the prison guards to join us.

11
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:03,420
He said they should not be stopped from studying for their degrees.

12
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:06,320
They were not cleverer than me,

13
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:08,240
but they did pass their exams.

14
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:11,180
So I knew I could get a degree too.

15
00:01:11,540 --> 00:01:14,100
That made me feel good about myself.

16
00:01:15,020 --> 00:01:16,960
When I finished the four years in prison,

17
00:01:16,960 --> 00:01:18,840
I went to find a job.

18
00:01:19,620 --> 00:01:23,940
Since I was better educated, I got a job working in an office.

19
00:01:24,540 --> 00:01:28,300
However, the police found out and told my boss that I had been in prison

20
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:30,220
for blowing up government buildings.

21
00:01:30,740 --> 00:01:32,600
So I lost my job.

22
00:01:40,940 --> 00:01:46,620
All that time my wife and children had to beg for food and help from relatives or friends.

23
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:54,580
Luckily Mr Mandela remembered me and gave me a job taking tourists around my old prison on Robben Island.

24
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:57,660
I felt bad the first time I talked to a group.

25
00:01:58,480 --> 00:02:01,780
All the terror and fear of that time came back to me.

26
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:07,220
I remembered the beatings and the cruelty of the guards and my friends who

27
00:02:07,220 --> 00:02:07,880
had died.

28
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:11,140
I felt I would not be able to do it,

29
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:13,520
but my family encouraged me.

30
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:18,920
They said that the job and the pay from the new South African government were my reward

31
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:22,140
after working all my life for equal rights for the Blacks.
